# tests/llm-async, as an ENTRY (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): evaluating this
# directory yields the test's ARG TREE, which dev/run-test then runs.
#
# A WORKER TEST. Durable independent work is llm-step's: it queues a request,
# becomes idle, and a later turn is handed a deterministic completion notice.
# The client curried two turns and blocked on each; worker-common.sh curries
# them and polls the conversation ref, which is where the evidence lives anyway.
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/worker-test --worker1:@=worker.sh --bash:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --llm-step:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-step --stub:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-stub --tool:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test-tool --async:@=async.sh --common:@=DEEP-DEPS/llm-test/worker-common.sh
